    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras are positioned for a high-ceiling offensive output today, anchored by **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (80.98) and **Trea Turner** (79.40), who represent our strongest plays. Both benefit significantly from a prime matchup against Dobnak and Bieber, respectively; these opposing pitchers carry high xERA profiles that inflate our scoring potential. **Pete Crow-Armstrong** is our highest-rated starter, buoyed by an elite lead-off spot, a favorable platoon advantage, and weather conditions with wind blowing out. Similarly, **Kyle Schwarber** (78.21) remains a high-floor start in the same favorable environment against Bieber, capitalizing on a top-of-the-order boost and a significant skill advantage against the opposing starter.\n\nStrategic lineup construction forced a difficult decision regarding **Josh Smith**, who fell just short of our 40.0 floor with a 32.43 efficiency rating. Despite the relative boost from facing Luzardo, **Josh Smith** was sidelined due to a negative platoon split and a low-leverage batting position (8th), making him the most viable candidate for benching as we aim to preserve our daily game caps. While **Yordan Alvarez** (65.05) maintains a strong projection despite his \"Lineup Pending\" status, we are monitoring the situation closely; should he be scratched, we have depth ready to minimize the impact. Finally, while **Kazuma Okamoto** (47.92), **Colt Keith** (52.60), and **Carson Benge** (47.50) are all starting, they face stiffer competition against tough arms like Luzardo and Jones, keeping their scores in the mid-tier. We will continue to prioritize speed and situational advantages\u2014like the dynamic platoon edges enjoyed by **Gary Sanchez** and **Junior Caminero**\u2014to navigate the remaining schedule.",
